proofs={500:('refuted, with the refined statement’s id','CL-SA02-501; verification.md V01: squarefree-denominator module; all flatness/local exclusion hypotheses verified.'),501:('independent re-proof','verification.md V01: finite saturation, separating duals, countable split exhaustion.'),502:('independent re-proof','verification.md V02: torsionfree tensor-quotient argument and intersection.'),503:('independent re-proof','verification.md V02: algebra generators and counit; arbitrary algebra-valued points.'),505:('independent re-proof','verification.md V14: finite coefficient support and projective coalgebra duality.'),506:('independent re-proof','verification.md V14: finite free dual-algebra module covers; relative global statement remains conditional.'),508:('refuted, with the refined statement’s id','CL-SA02-503; verification.md V02 and exact matrix certificate C02.'),509:('targeted proof check','verification.md V14: dual-basis envelope under projective coalgebra assumptions; flat-only extension excluded.'),512:('refuted, with the refined statement’s id','CL-SA02-511; verification.md V03: infinite-dimensional module over a point.'),517:('targeted proof check','90/25: associated graded quotients by flatness, then induction on the Artinian filtration.'),525:('independent re-proof','Noetherian compact Hausdorff profinite space: every subset compact and closed, hence discrete and finite.'),526:('independent re-proof','Prime contractions give dimension zero; noetherian implies Artinian; finite-spectrum point separation proves eventual factor stabilization under injectivity.'),527:('targeted proof check','90/9: geometrically connected fibres plus fpqc quotient topology descend clopen subsets.'),528:('targeted proof check','90/7,15: open graph descent and descent of its projection isomorphism.'),529:('targeted proof check','Depth formula and DVR exceptional case checked; Hartshorne connectedness theorem used as reference rather than reproved.'),532:('refuted, with the refined statement’s id','CL-SA02-531 gives the applicable connected-fibre corollary. Universal catenarity is not equivalent to geometrically reduced formal fibres; EGA IV4 18.9.9 uses universally Japanese.'),535:('targeted proof check','91/7: flatness preserves schematic density, giving equality with a closed subscheme containing X_U.')}
